  "text": "Recipe: Dhokla\nCreator: Mrs N K Manku\nCategory: Chaat\nIngredients: chana dal, hing (asafoetida), beetroot, onion, carrot, green beans, ginger, green chili, black pepper, garlic powder, raw mango powder, mustard seeds, curry leaves, white sesame seeds, date paste, lemon juice, mint leaves, raisins, dried berries, Green Chutney\nCooking methods: no-cook, blend, steam, roast, boil\nInstructions: SOAK & FERMENT: Soak 1/2 cup chana dal for 4 hours. Drain water, grind it with 1/4 tsp hing (asafoetida). Add water if required but not more than 1 or 2 tsp. Keep it for 8 to 10 hours for fermentation.\nBATTER: Add 1/2 cup of finely chopped Rainbow Vegetables of your choice: beetroot, onion, carrot, green beans. Add finely minced ginger (a small piece), 1/2 green chili, 1/4 tsp black pepper, 1/4 tsp garlic powder, 1/2 tsp anchor (raw mango powder). Mix all the ingredients.\nSTEAM: Transfer the batter to a container: small bowls. Steam for 20 to 25 minutes.\nTADKA: Dry roast 1/2 tsp mustard seeds, 4-5 five curry leaves, 3 to 4 green chillis, 1/4 tsp white sesame seeds, 1/2 tsp date paste, 1/2 tsp lemon juice. Boil for 2 to 3 minutes.\nSERVE: Remove dhokla from bowls. Pour TADKA on dhokla. Garnish with mint leaves, raisins, some dried berries. Serve with Green Chutney.\nNotes: Green Chutney",
